# phenylphosphonic_acid.msf
# Phenylphosphonic acid (PhP(O)(OH)2)
# pKa1=1.830 (first P-OH, q=0→-1)  pKa2=7.070 (second P-OH, q=-1→-2)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# Aryl phosphonate bridges methylphosphonic acid (err=+1.96) and inorganic
# phosphoric acid. The phenyl ring changes the BO descriptor pattern
# substantially vs methyl: ΔBO_ring is active, ΔBO_XC(P-C) is different.
# pKa1=1.83 fills the very-low-pKa region with a new phosphonate example.

